'''Ominira International Airport''' (also known as '''Iacob Kheme International Airport''', {{airport codes|OBK|BKOB}}) is the main international airport of the [[Bolodun and Kuvari Islands]], serving the capital [[Ominira]]. It is located on the eastern half of the island of [[Bolodun]], away from the city, and connected to Ominira by road across the island.

== History ==

The airport was originally built in the colonial era. In 1969, [[Hurricane Sahan]] destroyed virtually the entire island, including the airport. It was reconstructed on 15 March 1971 as part of the [[Adonian Community]]-led rebuilding of Bolodun, with hurricane-resistant construction paid for in part by heavy Burawi investment in the 1970s.

== Facilities ==

The airport has a single runway, 11,870 feet (3,618 metres) long, aligned diagonally with the coast in a roughly NW–SE orientation (runway 14/32). It has one terminal building.

Like many other structures in Ominira and on Bolodun, the airport is built on stilts, raised above the ground. It was constructed with hurricane-proof windows and an advanced drainage system so that the airport can quickly return to operation after a hurricane passes. The raised design keeps terminal facilities and utilities above storm surge and flood level.

